       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The maximum is 2,000 mg/day for many extended-release products.\n- **Risk:** The order is twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily, or\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, titrated up if the patient is newly starting metformin.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note to add to the order."
